; A balance assertion naming a lot still matches the lot when
; --value-expr, --account-value-expr or --commodity-value-expr gives the
; lot its valuation, though the journal itself names none.
;
; Each option's expression goes to the lot itself, which every amount of
; the lot shares, and the lot still answers to the name it was bought
; under, so the assertion's 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01], written without
; the valuation, names the valued lot.  3.4.1 had neither
; --account-value-expr nor --commodity-value-expr, and under --value-expr
; it rejected the assertion, as it checked balance assertions against
; the account's holdings stripped of their lot annotations (#2318,
; #2355): "Balance assertion off by 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))
; (expected to see 0)".

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 AAPL @ $5
    Assets:Cash

2020/01/02 Check
    Assets:Broker    0 AAPL = 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]

test --value-expr '$7' bal --lots Assets:Broker
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))  Assets:Broker
end test

test --account-value-expr '$7' bal --lots Assets:Broker
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))  Assets:Broker
end test

test --commodity-value-expr '$7' bal --lots Assets:Broker
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))  Assets:Broker
end test
